1
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:12,260
Buzz buzz

2
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:16,140
Buzz buzz. I've reached my limit today!

3
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:18,020
Hey,

4
00:00:21,780 --> 00:00:23,120
See how you like it?

5
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:25,140
Ryo-chan, what are you doing?

6
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:26,620
Can't you see?

7
00:00:26,620 --> 00:00:30,580
I'm venting all the pent-up frustration
I've built up toward the Chief.

8
00:00:30,580 --> 00:00:33,680
You made this diorama just for that?

9
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:36,300
Even I'm not that free.

10
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:38,960
I started by building this tank.

11
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:42,140
So then I wanted a diorama
for the background too.

12
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:44,640
That's why I built this police box.

13
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:48,420
In that case,
we can't start without the Chief, right?

14
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:50,900
How pathetic. You have plenty of free time.

15
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:56,780
Building models like this takes an incredible
amount of patience and concentration.

16
00:00:56,780 --> 00:01:01,080
Look closely at this diorama,
recreated in realistic detail.

17
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:03,720
It really is well made.

18
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:07,960
But then, out of nowhere,
a tank comes crashing in here!

19
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:09,080
How awful!

20
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:10,660
The Chief runs away!

21
00:01:10,660 --> 00:01:13,160
Go, tank of justice!

22
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,260
Because I'm going to crush Chief Ohara,

23
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:17,760
you'll get what's coming to you.

24
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:20,640
Is he always doing stuff like this?

25
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:22,080
Nyahahaha!

26
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:23,600
Serves you right!

27
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:25,120
You seem to be having a lot of fun.

28
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:27,120
Hey, Chief.

29
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:28,440
Ryotsu.

30
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:30,740
You bastard!

31
00:01:30,740 --> 00:01:32,620
Sorry, sorry.

32
00:01:33,420 --> 00:01:35,440
Building this worthless junk while on duty!

33
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:37,620
Get rid of this junk.

34
00:01:37,620 --> 00:01:38,920
Aaaaah!

35
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:40,680
My Dioramen...

36
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:41,820
From now on, no exceptions.

37
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:44,620
No building plastic models
inside the police box!

38
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:45,860
N-no way!

39
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:54,180
When you watch TV,
turn on the lights and sit farther back.

40
00:02:03,980 --> 00:02:07,340
On a morning you're broke, come to my place.

41
00:02:07,340 --> 00:02:11,980
I'm broke too, so don't worry.

42
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:19,300
Look at the blue sky, the white clouds.

43
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:25,720
It'll all work out somehow.

44
00:02:27,640 --> 00:02:31,020
You get it, right? Right, right.

45
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:34,960
Once you understand, just quietly follow me.

46
00:02:47,780 --> 00:02:51,360
Top-secret mission in 50 knots

47
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:55,620
You summoned me, Police Commissioner?

48
00:02:57,060 --> 00:03:00,460
The truth is, we've landed in
a terribly serious situation.

49
00:03:00,980 --> 00:03:02,820
A terribly serious

50
00:03:02,820 --> 00:03:04,320
W-what is it?

51
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:05,260
That is...

52
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:08,860
You see,

53
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:14,820
I need you to appraise
this within two weeks.

54
00:03:16,540 --> 00:03:19,300
This is a model of the
Hōryū-ji five-story pagoda.

55
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:25,260
That's right. No matter what, I have to
complete this within two weeks, or I...

56
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:32,720
Surely there's some serious behind-the-scenes
situation with this that even we can't talk about...

57
00:03:33,740 --> 00:03:36,100
Yes, it must be exactly that.

58
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:38,720
Leave it to me, Commissioner.

59
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:41,540
I will take full responsibility
and accept this task.

60
00:03:41,540 --> 00:03:44,160
Is that so? I'm counting on you.

61
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:51,240
The Commissioner's expression just now...
that was no ordinary matter.

62
00:03:52,060 --> 00:03:55,220
But I've never assembled
anything like this before.

63
00:03:55,220 --> 00:03:57,140
So what should I do?

64
00:03:58,380 --> 00:03:59,920
Right, excuse me.

65
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:01,920
You called for me, Commissioner?

66
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:06,240
Actually, I need you to assemble this.

67
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:08,100
This one?

68
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:13,120
That's right. No matter what,
you must complete this within two weeks.

69
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:18,040
I'm warning you, if this isn't finished,
then we won't have a tomorrow.

70
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:24,040
It's fine, leave it to me.

71
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:26,020
Count on you.

72
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:28,320
You called for me, Commissioner?

73
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:32,740
Actually, I need you to assemble this.

74
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:35,080
This one?

75
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:38,500
I've never built anything like this.

76
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:42,400
No, I'm not saying I
want you to assemble it.

77
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:44,820
You have someone under you, don't you?

78
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:47,140
Someone who's good at this sort of thing.

79
00:04:47,140 --> 00:04:50,460
You don't mean Ryotsu, do you?

80
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:52,180
Exactly.

81
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:55,220
A model like this is nothing for him, right?

82
00:04:55,220 --> 00:04:58,280
Why don't you ask Ryotsu for it?

83
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:00,960
From now on, absolutely not.

84
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:03,800
Building plastic models inside
the police box is banned.

85
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:04,560
No way...

86
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:07,560
After what I said earlier,

87
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:09,660
it's awkward for me to be the one asking,

88
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:11,860
but please, Ohara-kun.

89
00:05:11,860 --> 00:05:14,880
This is a mission the
Commissioner personally requested.

90
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:17,300
And if this isn't completed,

91
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:18,680
you and I

92
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:20,180
W-what?!

93
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:23,100
Judging by the Commissioner's manner,

94
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:26,920
there's serious backstory to
this that we don't know about.

95
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:30,080
If we botch this, we'll never get promoted.

96
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:34,400
No, we might not even have
jobs starting tomorrow.

97
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,280
Keep that in mind.

98
00:05:36,740 --> 00:05:38,920
Eeh... understood.

99
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:45,220
Ryo-chan, you were still hiding this?

100
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:46,500
Of course I was.

101
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:50,620
I'm not the type to give up just
because the chief told me to quit.

102
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:52,180
Alright, let's build it!

103
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:53,460
Yo!

104
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:56,360
M-my goodness!

105
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:58,070
Well, you see,

106
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:03,180
I dropped a pencil in the pond earlier, and a goddess appeared
and rewarded me for being honest, or something like that.

107
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:04,667
Kushii...

108
00:06:04,717 --> 00:06:08,100
I'm assigning you a critical mission.

109
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:11,080
Assemble this for me.

110
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:12,580
What's this?

111
00:06:12,900 --> 00:06:15,070
It's a model of a five-story pagoda

112
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:17,340
Isn't this wooden?

113
00:06:17,340 --> 00:06:20,900
It's a full-scale one,
over one meter when completed.

114
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:22,540
This is the important assignment?

115
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:25,740
Yes, that's exactly why I'm asking you.

116
00:06:25,740 --> 00:06:28,820
Because you're an idiot
who's only good in this field.

117
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:30,960
Idiot.

118
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:34,600
It's a direct request from the station chief,
so do it properly, Ryotsu.

119
00:06:36,140 --> 00:06:38,160
It's Ryotsu-san, right?

120
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:41,640
Why the hell should I add "-san" to you?

121
00:06:42,460 --> 00:06:45,840
I see. Well then, good work.

122
00:06:47,340 --> 00:06:50,200
Fine, please, Mr. Ryotsu.

123
00:06:54,660 --> 00:06:56,120
Ryotsu-san

124
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:58,600
I can't quite hear you.

125
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:01,060
Ryotsu-san

126
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:05,860
Adding "-san" when asking someone for a favor is common sense,
you know.

127
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:07,820
Do you understand, Ohara-kun?

128
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:11,080
Understood, Ryotsu-san. Please do it.

129
00:07:12,280 --> 00:07:15,680
But I'm busy with all sorts of things,
you know.

130
00:07:17,340 --> 00:07:18,820
What was my schedule like?

131
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:20,590
Nap around noon,

132
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:23,380
snack at three,
bath at six, dinner at seven.

133
00:07:23,380 --> 00:07:26,160
That's a hard schedule.

134
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:28,200
How much do you want?

135
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:30,320
What did you say?

136
00:07:30,620 --> 00:07:33,160
I'm asking how much you want, exactly!

137
00:07:33,860 --> 00:07:35,460
Come on, Chief, really.

138
00:07:35,460 --> 00:07:38,400
That makes it sound like
I'm blackmailing you.

139
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:40,100
It's outright blackmail.

140
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:44,320
This model is priced at
85,000 yen before tax, right?

141
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:46,160
So what?

142
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:49,780
Finished ones were being
sold for 700,000 yen.

143
00:07:50,820 --> 00:07:51,860
700,000 yen.

144
00:07:51,860 --> 00:07:55,820
Hansen models going for a
million yen finished is common.

145
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:59,280
That's how high the level of
craftsmanship and skill is.

146
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:01,600
I didn't know that.

147
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:04,620
But since it's a request from the Chief,
of all people,

148
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:06,640
I'll make it for you for 50,000 yen.

149
00:08:06,640 --> 00:08:08,460
Really? Thank you.

150
00:08:08,460 --> 00:08:10,700
Quoting a high price at first,

151
00:08:10,700 --> 00:08:12,380
is a trick to make it seem cheap.

152
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:14,500
Ryo-chan's good at haggling, isn't he?

153
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:16,480
Rest assured, Chief.

154
00:08:17,340 --> 00:08:19,300
Leave it to Kankichi Ryotsu.

155
00:08:20,340 --> 00:08:21,480
I'm counting on you, Ryotsu.

156
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:24,460
Ryotsu-san.

157
00:08:24,460 --> 00:08:25,600
Yeah, yeah.

158
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:32,580
I see. So you'll take it on.

159
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:34,380
Just as I'd expect from you, Ohara.

160
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:38,240
I'm proud to have a subordinate like you.

161
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:41,660
My judgment in asking you
was not wrong after all.

162
00:08:41,660 --> 00:08:42,880
I'm counting on you.

163
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:45,540
Good morning.

164
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:46,780
Morning.

165
00:08:47,340 --> 00:08:49,640
Is the five-story pagoda's
construction progressing?

166
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:51,000
So it seems.

167
00:08:51,540 --> 00:08:53,460
So it's finally time to assemble it?

168
00:08:53,460 --> 00:08:55,560
As expected, you're quick about it.

169
00:08:56,580 --> 00:09:00,100
Hey, Chief,
I've already covered this money for you.

170
00:09:01,940 --> 00:09:04,500
What's this? A bill for 150,000 yen?

171
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:06,000
It's an expense report.

172
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,640
Why are the expenses so high?

173
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:11,840
I bought everything I needed
for building the model.

174
00:09:11,840 --> 00:09:14,180
Comb set, electric drill

175
00:09:14,180 --> 00:09:15,900
Gas burner for weathering

176
00:09:17,340 --> 00:09:18,320
Electronic organizer

177
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,600
Potato chips and Calorie Mate

178
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:20,240
Whiskey

179
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:20,860
Shampoo

180
00:09:20,860 --> 00:09:21,540
Underwear

181
00:09:21,540 --> 00:09:22,040
Soap

182
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:22,560
Toothbrush

183
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:24,260
Manga and video games

184
00:09:24,260 --> 00:09:25,600
And cup noodles.

185
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:26,340
Hold it!

186
00:09:26,340 --> 00:09:28,980
The second half is all unnecessary stuff!

187
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:31,420
I'm not paying for that crap!

188
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:35,060
Then are you going to
assemble this yourself, Chief?

189
00:09:38,260 --> 00:09:40,260
I just remembered I have something to do.

190
00:09:40,260 --> 00:09:41,460
I'm heading home...

191
00:09:41,460 --> 00:09:42,660
W-wait!

192
00:09:42,660 --> 00:09:43,680
Fine.

193
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:44,720
I'll do as you say.

194
00:09:44,720 --> 00:09:46,840
So keep working on it, please.

195
00:09:47,340 --> 00:09:49,500
Good, that's all I needed to hear.

196
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:52,100
This job takes a lot of nerve, you know.

197
00:09:52,540 --> 00:09:54,120
S-sorry, I was wrong.

198
00:09:54,120 --> 00:09:57,020
After all,
you're the only one who can build it.

199
00:09:57,020 --> 00:09:58,440
Please do your best.

200
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:01,680
I have no idea how much this
will cost before it's finished.

201
00:10:01,680 --> 00:10:03,220
Poor Chief.

202
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:06,660
If you need anything,
don't hesitate to tell me.

203
00:10:06,660 --> 00:10:08,260
I'll arrange it right away.

204
00:10:09,140 --> 00:10:10,820
I'm getting a little hungry.

205
00:10:10,820 --> 00:10:12,480
I want some unaju.

206
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:13,760
O-okay.

207
00:10:14,340 --> 00:10:16,220
Nakagawa, order some unaju!

208
00:10:16,220 --> 00:10:16,560
Yes.

209
00:10:17,340 --> 00:10:19,220
The one from that old restaurant in Ueno.

210
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:20,760
Don't joke around.

211
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:24,160
Of course they won't
deliver from Ueno to Kameari!

212
00:10:24,160 --> 00:10:27,060
Couldn't we just ride a bike and pick it up?

213
00:10:27,060 --> 00:10:28,020
Hey, Chief.

214
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:29,680
Y-you...

215
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:32,180
I'm quite picky about flavor, you know.

216
00:10:32,680 --> 00:10:33,320
*Squeeze...*

217
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:35,540
Fine, I'll go buy it.

218
00:10:36,060 --> 00:10:38,680
That was good.

219
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:42,580
It was worth having the Chief
go out of his way to buy it.

220
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:42,900
Hey.

221
00:10:44,940 --> 00:10:47,080
Now my shoulders are a bit stiff.

222
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:49,160
I wish someone would massage them.

223
00:10:49,160 --> 00:10:50,340
Someone...

224
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:54,740
Sorry.

225
00:10:54,740 --> 00:10:56,840
A mosquito landed on it, so...

226
00:10:59,280 --> 00:11:00,740
Oops, damn it.

227
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:02,920
Well, that's a problem.

228
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:05,160
Time to reassemble it again.

229
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:07,520
Will we make the deadline?

230
00:11:07,520 --> 00:11:08,860
It's getting dangerous.

231
00:11:08,860 --> 00:11:10,680
Please do your best.

232
00:11:12,580 --> 00:11:14,280
And call me "sensei."

233
00:11:14,280 --> 00:11:16,240
Hahahaha!

234
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:19,660
Morning.

235
00:11:19,660 --> 00:11:21,340
Good morning.

236
00:11:21,340 --> 00:11:23,380
What, Ryotsu isn't here yet?

237
00:11:23,380 --> 00:11:24,860
W-well, you see...

238
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:27,672
To add more realism,

239
00:11:27,722 --> 00:11:29,620
I'm heading out for on-site research.

240
00:11:29,620 --> 00:11:33,200
Please cover the transportation
and other expenses, Chief.

241
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:34,040
Ryotsu!

242
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:38,160
On-site research...
you don't mean... n-no way...

243
00:11:38,160 --> 00:11:41,200
Did that guy actually make
it all the way to Nara alive?

244
00:11:44,020 --> 00:11:47,040
Hehehehe

245
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:50,760
Making the models is the best!

246
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:53,820
Even the chief who nags me all
the time is at my beck and call now.

247
00:11:54,260 --> 00:11:57,700
In that case, I'll push back the
completion right up to the deadline.

248
00:11:57,700 --> 00:12:00,380
I'm going to milk the
chief for everything I can.

249
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:04,000
I'm back.

250
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:06,140
Ryotsu, you...

251
00:12:07,223 --> 00:12:10,980
Who do you think you're calling
"kisama," Chief?

252
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:11,920
Shut up.

253
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:17,580
I won't ask you anymore.
Where are you going? To the chief's office.

254
00:12:18,160 --> 00:12:26,440
To the chief's office. I can't stand it anymore!
Ohara-kun, how can you stay so calm about this?

255
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:33,980
Ryotsu is running wild, claiming only
he can assemble that five-story pagoda.

256
00:12:33,980 --> 00:12:34,980
I-I see.

257
00:12:34,980 --> 00:12:37,740
For now,
let's try talking to the Commissioner.

258
00:12:38,460 --> 00:12:39,480
The Commissioner?

259
00:12:40,060 --> 00:12:41,060
Excuse me.

260
00:12:41,060 --> 00:12:42,740
Commissioner, I have something to discuss.

261
00:12:43,580 --> 00:12:45,580
What? You're saying the
five-story pagoda is impossible?

262
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:47,280
I'm terribly sorry.

263
00:12:47,280 --> 00:12:49,960
However,
according to reports from those on site,

264
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:52,320
it's apparently running
into serious difficulties.

265
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:54,020
This is bad.

266
00:12:54,020 --> 00:12:55,440
That's bad.

267
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:57,960
If that isn't finished, I...

268
00:12:59,460 --> 00:13:01,260
That grave expression.

269
00:13:01,260 --> 00:13:03,860
There must be something
serious behind this matter,

270
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:07,300
d-don't tell me it's a crisis
for the nation's survival?

271
00:13:07,300 --> 00:13:09,900
Could the future of Japan's
police force be at stake?

272
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:12,180
Understood, Commissioner.

273
00:13:12,180 --> 00:13:15,720
You needn't say another word.
Leave everything to me.

274
00:13:16,140 --> 00:13:16,680
Please.

275
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:19,400
Somehow, get the five-story pagoda finished.

276
00:13:19,820 --> 00:13:20,180
I see.

277
00:13:20,820 --> 00:13:23,980
So the one behind the request
was the Commissioner himself.

278
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:27,420
Now this is getting interesting.

279
00:13:36,060 --> 00:13:37,680
This is a masterpiece.

280
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:39,800
Ryotsu!

281
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:43,940
If you think I'll keep groveling forever,
you've got another thing coming!

282
00:13:45,020 --> 00:13:49,420
If the five-story pagoda isn't finished,
the Chief will be in trouble, won't he?

283
00:13:50,300 --> 00:13:51,600
How did you...

284
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:55,600
And on top of that, the one who commissioned it from
the Chief is the Police Commissioner General, no less.

285
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:59,100
This might mean I can't
stay in the police force.

286
00:13:59,100 --> 00:14:03,100
What? The Commissioner General?
That's absurd!

287
00:14:04,680 --> 00:14:08,600
Hello, yes, please hold for a moment.

288
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:10,360
Chief, you have a phone call.

289
00:14:10,360 --> 00:14:11,660
Who is it?

290
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:13,140
Well, it's...

291
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:17,320
Yes, this is Ohara speaking.

292
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:20,100
G-G-Commissioner General!

293
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:23,120
Yes, no, that's not...

294
00:14:23,760 --> 00:14:26,183
No, but...

295
00:14:26,233 --> 00:14:29,060
Yes, I understand.

296
00:14:29,620 --> 00:14:31,200
Yes, goodbye.

297
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:36,180
The Commissioner's tense demeanor,

298
00:14:36,180 --> 00:14:39,940
there must be a very important
reason behind this, right?

299
00:14:41,580 --> 00:14:43,920
So if we mess this up,

300
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:48,360
you, me, the Chief,
and the Station Chief might all be fired.

301
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:50,420
That's too bad.

302
00:14:50,880 --> 00:14:51,800
Understood.

303
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:53,020
Understood.

304
00:14:53,020 --> 00:14:54,760
Please somehow get it assembled.

305
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:55,640
Mr. Ryotsu,

306
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:58,920
Leave it to me, Ohara.

307
00:14:59,100 --> 00:14:59,620
Come on.

308
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:03,220
Hey, Ryo-chan, isn't this a bit much?

309
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:07,140
Taking advantage of people's weaknesses is the senior officer's specialty,
after all.

310
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:11,840
But at this rate, the five-story
pagoda will never get finished.

311
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:15,180
There's no telling how much the chief
and the others will end up paying.

312
00:15:16,060 --> 00:15:16,460
Yeah, you're right.

313
00:15:17,160 --> 00:15:20,220
Ryotsu-sama,
is there anything else you need?

314
00:15:20,560 --> 00:15:24,880
Let's see, I'd like about twenty
of Urashimaya's bean-jam buns.

315
00:15:28,380 --> 00:15:30,240
Yes, I'll go buy them right away.

316
00:15:31,740 --> 00:15:33,740
Chief, I'd like a word with you.

317
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:36,800
Not here, though.

318
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:42,500
A model-kit champion, no less?

319
00:15:42,500 --> 00:15:46,560
Yes, the runner-up of last year's
world model contest
,

320
00:15:46,560 --> 00:15:49,280
was working at our company's branch in Russia,
so

321
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:51,500
we immediately brought him back to Japan.

322
00:15:51,900 --> 00:15:53,640
He'll arrive at Narita tomorrow.

323
00:15:54,880 --> 00:15:58,780
If we leave the five-story pagoda to him, we
won't have to do Ryo-chan's bidding anymore.

324
00:15:58,780 --> 00:16:00,400
I see.

325
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:03,580
Hehehe, just you wait, Ryotsu,

326
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:06,000
your reign ends today!

327
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,780
Hahahahaha!

328
00:16:08,420 --> 00:16:11,700
Nakagawa's getting worried.
I've got to do something about this.

329
00:16:18,700 --> 00:16:21,800
Someone should have come to greet us by now.

330
00:16:21,800 --> 00:16:24,320
Ahahaha! Welcome!

331
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:28,280
World model contest runner-up,
Alexei Plamoskii!

332
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:29,300
Who's that?!

333
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:31,820
I'm not giving my name to the likes of you!

334
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:35,120
Yay! Plamoskii!

335
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:38,380
This is sudden,
but I challenge you to a model duel!

336
00:16:38,820 --> 00:16:40,000
A model duel?

337
00:16:40,320 --> 00:16:42,840
That's right!
I'm no slouch with a model kit myself!

338
00:16:42,940 --> 00:16:44,760
I won't lose to the likes of you!

339
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:47,120
Interesting! I'll take you on!

340
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:53,360
Alright, we'll decide this match on the
completeness of the 1/250 Mobile Force Gangar.

341
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:56,600
Bring it on! Then, model fight!

342
00:16:56,600 --> 00:16:58,480
Ready, go!

343
00:17:08,840 --> 00:17:09,760
Its eyes light up!

344
00:17:12,480 --> 00:17:15,260
Nobody will be impressed by
such a plain modification!

345
00:17:15,260 --> 00:17:16,920
Look at mine.

346
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:19,420
By modifying the joints,

347
00:17:19,420 --> 00:17:22,320
it's possible to strike any pose you want.

348
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:24,380
Its upper arms can fly off!

349
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:27,800
Then its legs fly off!

350
00:17:29,860 --> 00:17:31,620
And then even its head,

351
00:17:34,300 --> 00:17:36,920
and even its body can fly off!

352
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:42,080
I lost.

353
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:47,120
He should be arriving about now.

354
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:50,440
Hey, where's Mr. Plamoskii?

355
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:55,100
And my model, such as it is,

356
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:57,620
What happened to Mr. Plamoskii?

357
00:17:58,460 --> 00:18:00,960
I'm still an inexperienced fool.

358
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:03,200
I'll go home and start over.

359
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:08,240
What on earth happened?

360
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,840
So he just went home?

361
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:14,520
Yes, he seemed completely crushed somehow.

362
00:18:14,520 --> 00:18:18,500
Well, there's no help for it.
Let's try someone else.

363
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:23,380
Hey, hey, hey!
You're the modeler Chin Zōkei, aren't you?

364
00:18:23,380 --> 00:18:25,360
Let's have a fair fight!

365
00:18:28,820 --> 00:18:30,000
I lost.

366
00:18:30,860 --> 00:18:34,600
You're still not there yet.
Go home and train from the very beginning.

367
00:18:38,900 --> 00:18:40,584
Hahahaha!

368
00:18:40,634 --> 00:18:43,140
I never imagined there was such a method.

369
00:18:43,140 --> 00:18:46,340
He picked the wrong opponent, hahahaha!

370
00:18:46,840 --> 00:18:50,400
I-I don't understand it.
Using something like that in a model kit!

371
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:54,218
Trying to beat me is three
hundred million years too early,

372
00:18:54,268 --> 00:18:55,300
hahaha.

373
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:58,400
What? They've all gone home?

374
00:18:58,400 --> 00:19:01,820
But don't worry,
another one is coming today.

375
00:19:02,500 --> 00:19:03,360
Really?

376
00:19:03,360 --> 00:19:06,560
Yes, this time Kei-chan is guarding him.

377
00:19:06,560 --> 00:19:08,320
He'll definitely be fine.

378
00:19:08,860 --> 00:19:12,400
I see. Good. Ryotsu's reign ends here.

379
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:22,640
Mister Modeler, I'm counting on
you for the five-story pagoda.

380
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:27,120
Leave it to me. I'll recreate a five-story
pagoda that looks just like the real thing.

381
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:28,820
What is that?

382
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:36,560
Senpai, so you're the world model contest champion,
Ken Modera.

383
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:40,840
As long as I have breath in my body,
I won't let you act big here in Japan!

384
00:19:40,840 --> 00:19:42,900
Now then, let's have a fair model battle!

385
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:47,540
I see, so all the people before
were sent packing by you, Senpai?

386
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:50,920
Mister Modeler,
let's head to a different heliport for now.

387
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:55,420
Non, non, non. If you run away when challenged,
you're not fit to be a modeler.

388
00:19:55,420 --> 00:19:57,980
Very well, I accept that challenge.

389
00:19:58,340 --> 00:20:04,900
What on earth are these modeler people?

390
00:20:06,560 --> 00:20:07,480
I won!

391
00:20:08,140 --> 00:20:09,740
What's this model dojo nonsense?

392
00:20:09,740 --> 00:20:11,420
I'm taking this sign with me.

393
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:16,300
Ozaru-meshi Ryotsu Kankichi

394
00:20:22,960 --> 00:20:24,220
An unbeaten streak!

395
00:20:24,220 --> 00:20:26,920
There's no one left in the
country who can challenge me.

396
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:27,660
Senpai

397
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:31,080
You came back again,
never learning your lesson.

398
00:20:31,080 --> 00:20:34,540
No matter who comes, I will never lose.

399
00:20:35,600 --> 00:20:37,480
Is it really all right to be doing that?

400
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:40,360
Ryo-chan,
haven't you forgotten something important?

401
00:20:40,980 --> 00:20:42,380
Something important?

402
00:20:43,800 --> 00:20:44,720
50 of 10

403
00:20:44,720 --> 00:20:46,260
Oh no!

404
00:20:46,260 --> 00:20:49,320
I got so caught up in the model
battle that I completely forgot.

405
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:51,180
It's due tomorrow, you know.

406
00:20:51,180 --> 00:20:52,320
What are you going to do?

407
00:20:53,240 --> 00:20:54,580
If it isn't finished,

408
00:20:54,580 --> 00:20:55,860
you won't get off lightly.

409
00:20:55,860 --> 00:20:57,620
You won't get off lightly.

410
00:20:57,620 --> 00:21:00,220
You idiot!

411
00:21:00,220 --> 00:21:04,740
This is bad.

412
00:21:04,740 --> 00:21:07,280
We're going to finish it
by tomorrow no matter what!

413
00:21:09,340 --> 00:21:10,440
Come on, come on, come on!

414
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:12,720
You're like a kid who played
too much during summer vacation.

415
00:21:13,740 --> 00:21:14,720
You can do it, so

416
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:20,220
I did it!

417
00:21:21,820 --> 00:21:23,500
I somehow made it in time.

418
00:21:23,500 --> 00:21:26,040
All that's left is to take this over.

419
00:21:27,740 --> 00:21:28,620
Hello?

420
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:29,600
Chief.

421
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:30,680
Perfect timing.

422
00:21:30,680 --> 00:21:32,760
It was just completed.

423
00:21:32,760 --> 00:21:33,540
I see.

424
00:21:33,540 --> 00:21:34,440
Well done!

425
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:36,240
Then, by 1 o'clock today,

426
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:38,460
bring it to the
Commissioner-General's residence.

427
00:21:38,460 --> 00:21:39,600
Leave it to me.

428
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:41,500
I'll definitely deliver it.

429
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:42,520
Don't worry.

430
00:21:45,380 --> 00:21:50,160
For all your complaining, meeting the
deadline like this is truly professional work.

431
00:21:52,080 --> 00:21:52,900
Uh-oh!

432
00:21:54,260 --> 00:21:55,340
That was close.

433
00:21:58,780 --> 00:22:01,880
Water, fire extinguisher, where is it?
Where is it?

434
00:22:05,560 --> 00:22:07,560
It's completely burned up.

435
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:12,180
What do we do? Even if we remake it now,
we won't make it in time.

436
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:16,720
So it's finally finished?

437
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:19,240
I can't wait to see it.

438
00:22:19,240 --> 00:22:20,760
Yes, that's right.

439
00:22:21,280 --> 00:22:22,620
Hey, is it still not ready?

440
00:22:22,620 --> 00:22:23,420
Yes.

441
00:22:23,420 --> 00:22:25,280
Hey, is it still not ready?

442
00:22:25,280 --> 00:22:25,880
Yes.

443
00:22:25,880 --> 00:22:29,600
Hey, Nakagawa, Ryotsu is really
going to be all right, isn't he?

444
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:30,900
I think so.

445
00:22:30,900 --> 00:22:34,680
He called this morning
asking to borrow a car.

446
00:22:34,680 --> 00:22:35,300
A car?

447
00:22:35,300 --> 00:22:38,760
Yes, he said he needs it to
transport the five-story pagoda.

448
00:22:38,760 --> 00:22:41,640
That's right, he said he's fine.

449
00:22:42,400 --> 00:22:43,360
He's fine.

450
00:22:43,740 --> 00:22:46,220
Alright, no problem, Commissioner.

451
00:22:51,600 --> 00:22:54,160
That's unmistakably a five-story pagoda.

452
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:55,640
So it's finally here.

453
00:22:58,920 --> 00:23:00,280
What on earth is this?

454
00:23:01,180 --> 00:23:03,780
It's a life-size five-story pagoda!

455
00:23:03,780 --> 00:23:06,320
Wow, a huge five-story pagoda!

456
00:23:06,320 --> 00:23:07,960
Grandpa, thank you!

457
00:23:09,800 --> 00:23:10,680
"Thank you,"

458
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:14,540
I asked my grandson what he
wanted for his birthday present,

459
00:23:14,540 --> 00:23:16,680
and he said he wanted a five-story pagoda.

460
00:23:16,680 --> 00:23:18,700
Since I'd said I'd buy him anything,

461
00:23:18,700 --> 00:23:21,220
I had no choice but to get one.

462
00:23:21,220 --> 00:23:23,120
Didn't I mention that?

463
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:24,660
You never told me that.

464
00:23:24,660 --> 00:23:28,220
Here's your order, delivered as requested.

465
00:23:28,220 --> 00:23:30,460
Could you stamp or sign here?

466
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:33,680
Right, then.

467
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:34,740
Wait.

468
00:23:34,740 --> 00:23:35,860
It's my place.

469
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:38,520
What on earth is going on?

470
00:23:38,520 --> 00:23:39,540
Here is the next news.

471
00:23:40,680 --> 00:23:43,820
A mysterious incident has occurred
in which 50 towers suddenly vanished.

472
00:23:44,320 --> 00:23:46,060
Who could be behind this?

473
00:23:46,060 --> 00:23:47,980
Or is it a natural phenomenon?

474
00:23:47,980 --> 00:23:50,000
Or is it some unknown cosmic power?

475
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:51,680
The mystery only deepens.

476
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:53,220
Yo!

477
00:23:54,940 --> 00:23:57,800
Look, your grandkid seems happy too.

478
00:23:57,800 --> 00:23:59,360
Isn't that great?

479
00:23:59,360 --> 00:23:59,920
Well, then.

480
00:24:01,300 --> 00:24:03,180
Baka-man!

481
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:18,800
Na na na na, na na na na, na na na na

482
00:24:18,800 --> 00:24:24,280
for those who play the
fool just for their looks

483
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:27,460
I probably don't want to be like that

484
00:24:27,460 --> 00:24:32,060
if I'm dawdling around at the corner

485
00:24:32,060 --> 00:24:34,400
the moon has run away

486
00:24:34,400 --> 00:24:38,160
because now isn't everything

487
00:24:38,160 --> 00:24:42,620
don't get too worked up over the me of today

488
00:24:42,620 --> 00:24:46,360
even if I fudge a little, tell a small lie

489
00:24:46,860 --> 00:24:50,520
sometimes while I'm helping someone

490
00:24:50,520 --> 00:24:52,520
Baby, do you know me?

491
00:24:52,580 --> 00:24:56,880
facing tomorrow with a nice spirit

492
00:24:58,060 --> 00:25:01,960
Don't lose heart, we'll do what needs doing.

493
00:25:01,960 --> 00:25:04,320
A cute state of mind.

494
00:25:04,320 --> 00:25:07,740
What's hard to understand is

495
00:25:08,860 --> 00:25:11,560
just because I want it to look that way.

496
00:25:12,900 --> 00:25:17,300
Isn't it better than just
changing how it looks?

497
00:25:19,320 --> 00:25:23,960
Nanananananana

498
00:25:28,600 --> 00:25:30,200
Even!

499
00:25:30,240 --> 00:25:32,900
Big brother bought some baby castella cakes.

500
00:25:34,320 --> 00:25:36,500
Eve, you're still such a child!

501
00:25:37,160 --> 00:25:38,420
You have something to say?

502
00:25:38,420 --> 00:25:40,740
Kekeke, you're getting married!

503
00:25:41,080 --> 00:25:46,560
Next time: Honda Shock,
Eve's Wedding, I'll go astray!

